'''JSW Energy Limited''' is an Indian [[Electricity infrastructure|power]] company engaged in power [[Electricity generation|generation]], [[Electric power transmission|transmission]] and [[Electric power industry|trading]]. It is part of [[JSW Group]].

== Power plants ==
* [[JSW Vijayanagar Power Station]], Toranagallu village in [[Bellary district]], [[Karnataka]]. It is a 1460 MW (2x130,4x300 MW) plant.<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://www.jsw.in/Energy/inner_subpage.php?id=1&mid=2sid=4#projectunderoperations |title=JSW |access-date=20 March 2014 |archive-date=20 March 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140320175006/http://www.jsw.in/Energy/inner_subpage.php?id=1&mid=2sid=4#projectunderoperations |url-status=dead }}</ref>
* [[JSW Ratnagiri Power Station]], Nandiwade village near Jaigad in [[Ratnagiri district]], [[Maharashtra]]. It is a 1200 MW (4x300 MW) plant.<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://www.jsw.in/Energy/inner_subpage.php?id=2&mid=2sid=4#projectunderoperations |title=JSW |access-date=20 March 2014 |archive-date=20 March 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140320172353/http://www.jsw.in/Energy/inner_subpage.php?id=2&mid=2sid=4#projectunderoperations |url-status=dead }}</ref>
* [[JSW Barmer Power Station]], Bhadresh village in [[Barmer district]], [[Rajasthan]]. It is a 1080 MW (8x135 MW) plant.<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://www.jsw.in/Energy/inner_subpage.php?id=3&mid=2sid=4#projectunderoperations |title=JSW |access-date=20 March 2014 |archive-date=20 March 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140320174850/http://www.jsw.in/Energy/inner_subpage.php?id=3&mid=2sid=4#projectunderoperations |url-status=dead }}</ref>
*[[Karcham Wangtoo Hydroelectric Plant]], [[Kinnaur district]], [[Himachal Pradesh]]. It is a 1,091 MW [[hydropower]] plant commissioned in 2011, acquired in 2015
* [[Baspa Valley|Baspa]]-II Hydroelectric Plant, [[Kinnaur district]], [[Himachal Pradesh]]. It is a 300 MW hydropower plant which was commissioned in 2003, acquired in 2015
*[[Vijayanagara district|Vijaynagar]] Solar Plant, [[Vijayanagara district|Vijaynagar]], [[Karnataka]].It is a 225 MW Solar power plant which was commissioned in 2022.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.livemint.com/companies/news/jsw-energy-starts-operations-at-225-mw-vijayanagar-solar-project-11649327080114.html|title=JSW Energy starts operations at vijaynagar solar plant|date=7 April 2022 }}</ref>
*In 2015, JSW Energy acquired two of [[Jaypee Group]]'s hydropower plants, with a combined capacity of 1,391 MW, for {{INR}}9,700 crore.<ref>{{cite news |title=JSW Energy buys JP Power's 2 hydro projects for Rs 9,700 crore |language=en |work=The Times of India |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/jsw-energy-buys-jp-powers-2-hydro-projects-for-rs-9700-crore/articleshow/48871298.cms |access-date=13 December 2022}}</ref>

